# S4 co-engineering (always on)

Before coding, read:

1. `CLAUDE.md` (mandatory for Claude Code and all agents)
2. `AGENTS.md`
3. `docs/AI_COENGINEERING_PLAN_TO_PRODUCTION.md`
4. Workspace `S4-TRADEASY-LOCKED-ROADMAP.md` and `S4-LOCKED-WORK-PLAN.md` when adding finance/stock/report features

## Process order

1. Requirement / plan
2. Data model
3. Project structure
4. Coding standards / reference patterns
5. Reuse kits / services / components
6. Implement (production only)
7. Review / refactor
8. QA
9. Fix bugs / mismatches
10. Deploy only if user explicitly asks

## Product rules

- Do not 1:1 copy Tradeasy menus; build locked modern hubs (Books, Stock Hub, Analytics, etc.)
- Do not ask the user to restate these instructions
- No fake APIs, placeholders, or stub UI
- Preserve offline sync, permissions, and existing invoice/stock behavior

## Professional output (anti-AI-tell)

- Code and UI must look like careful human senior-engineer work
- **No emoji** in UI, menus, toasts, prints, commits messages for this app, or new strings
- Do not reintroduce emoji removed from the codebase
- Avoid generic AI layout clichés when not already in the design system
- Small, purposeful diffs; match neighboring file style

## Scope

- Default work is `src/` React app
- `erp/` Django lock (`ARCHITECTURE_LOCK.md`) only when editing `erp/`
